\f0\fs24 \cf2 The grand salon offers a remarkable glimpse into how the original layout envisioned by the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers has been impeccably preserved. The fireplace, imposing and majestic, still commands the room as it once did, while the wall sconces and central chandelier, just as seen in historical photographs, continue to draw the eye. But perhaps the most astonishing feature is the upholstery: one of only two in the entire house, along with that of the Sala Bevilacqua, to have survived intact over time. This salon remains the vibrant heart of the home, a place where the splendor of the past endures and continues to move those who walk through it.}